scope core infrastructure -- the REDS ledger guard family, four reds closed, two rows booked and folded
status GREEN -- hot roster pass 176 green of 180, its one red the known detached-shell leg that reads GREEN from an ordinary shell; after two rebases the eleven intersecting guards re-verified green by name, including all seven ledger-spine guards, fold_shelf_link, index_row_bound, log_file_claim and living_pin_near_bound
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- one. %592's gate is false-safe by its subject filter and I can widen it in an hour, yet landing the record it would then demand reds log_file_claim, because that lap's work was superseded by a peer's broader pre-commit rule six the same day. A superseded parked lap has no lawful door: the record gate refuses to be satisfied by dropping evidence, and rightly. Does an abandoned lap get a named exit, or does its work land anyway?
